  "limitations": [
    "The blacklisted-recipient scenario is treated as a potential precondition; the impact is formalized only for that conditional scenario.",
    "The safety intent is encoded as a liveness obligation that payOut can reduce totalOwed; the impact's revert and non-decrease are represented as separate observable booleans rather than numeric totalOwed values because the report gives no numeric amounts.",
    "The impact is formalized as a liveness failure of payOut reducing totalOwed under the blacklisted-user scenario; the reclaim of USDC is represented via the totalOwed reduction obligation rather than a separate USDC balance symbol.",
    "Blacklisting is a potential condition; the rule is scoped to the scenario where it holds.",
    "The blacklisting is a potential condition between requestRedeem and claimRedeem; the rule encodes only the conditional scenario in which it holds.",
    "The refund-path availability is a qualitative Boolean; no numeric or structural definition is supplied by the report.",
    "The impact's absence-of-function claim is represented as a Boolean context symbol; it is not a core observable of the required_effect pattern.",
    "Whether the blacklisting occurs before or after fundRedemptions is not stated; only the between-requestRedeem-and-claimRedeem window is encoded.",
    "The redirect-to-non-blacklisted-address alternative is folded into the payout-completion Boolean rather than modeled as a separate address relation.",
    "The frozen-funds impact is encoded as a Boolean occurrence symbol because the report provides no numeric magnitude or balance identity for the frozen amount.",
    "The blacklist precondition is potential/conditional; the rule formalizes the report-supported conditional scenario rather than asserting blacklisting always occurs.",
    "Only the single frozen intent source intent_total_owed_reducible is formalized here; other intents for this impact are separate claims.",
    "The refund-path availability is encoded as a qualitative Boolean because the report gives no numeric or structural definition of the refund mechanism.",
    "The frozen-funds impact is treated as the negation of refund-path availability under the blacklisted scenario; the report's 'accounting stays balanced' clause is not separately modeled."
  ]
